# omx-strip as the hand-ported 0.2.0 plugin (A) and as a chain (B): A's every setting, as B sets it.
# Read by tools/test/strip-crosscheck.sh (tools/test/clap-crosscheck.c); a line is <A name>|<B names>[|<a>:<b> ...], or |<B name>|=<x>.
Trim|Trim
HPF|HPF
HPF Freq|HPF Freq
HPF Slope|HPF Slope
LPF|LPF
LPF Freq|LPF Freq
# above 0.6 of Nyquist at 44.1 and 48 kHz the low-pass takes omx-dsp's hand-over, which removes the passband lift (up to +19 dB near Nyquist) the hand-ported strip had: omx-dsp#105, #116, #119. Not compared above that corner.
@cap|LPF Freq|0.6|omx-dsp low-pass hand-over near Nyquist (#105, #116, #119)
LPF Slope|LPF Slope
Gate|Gate
# the hand-ported strip passed its threshold as both knee edges (a hard knee)
Gate Threshold|Gate Threshold,Gate Knee Start,Gate Knee End
Gate Ratio|Gate Ratio
Gate Range|Gate Range
Gate Attack|Gate Attack
Gate Release|Gate Release
EQ|EQ
EQ 1 Type|EQ 1 Type
